WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.296 --> 00:00:01.129
- Huh.

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:05.135
I got a little emotional when you asked me the question.

00:00:05.135 --> 00:00:07.635
(light music)

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:11.798
- Being a multi-racial Asian

00:00:11.798 --> 00:00:16.465
affects everything about my life, my culture is a mix of

00:00:16.991 --> 00:00:19.574
not just being black and Asian,

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:22.396
but also there's like a third thing

00:00:22.396 --> 00:00:24.139
that's not either of those.

00:00:24.139 --> 00:00:27.222
^- I haven't felt like I really fit in

00:00:27.226 --> 00:00:28.915
^with either one of my cultures,

00:00:28.915 --> 00:00:32.380
because I didn't really look like my mom or my dad.

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:34.436
- On one hand, I was able to experience

00:00:34.436 --> 00:00:37.687
some white privilege, and on the other hand,

00:00:37.687 --> 00:00:39.437
I experienced certain

00:00:39.694 --> 00:00:43.491
prejudices and stereotypes of also being Asian.

00:00:43.491 --> 00:00:47.269
- We grew up being referred to as "Hapa-haole,"

00:00:47.269 --> 00:00:51.083
^and as I grew it became more of a widely accepted term

00:00:51.083 --> 00:00:53.298
^for anyone who was part Asian.

00:00:53.298 --> 00:00:56.304
It's been appropriated by a broader audience.

00:00:56.304 --> 00:00:59.179
I have mixed feelings when I hear the term, "hapa,"

00:00:59.179 --> 00:01:01.845
at least there's a way to acknowledge

00:01:01.845 --> 00:01:05.386
that not everybody is just one thing or another.

00:01:05.386 --> 00:01:06.561
- People say, "Oh, you're white,

00:01:06.561 --> 00:01:07.926
because you're not acting black,

00:01:07.926 --> 00:01:10.685
or because these things that you do aren't black,

00:01:10.685 --> 00:01:11.752
they must be white."

00:01:11.752 --> 00:01:13.891
And that's annoying because I'm not white either.

00:01:13.891 --> 00:01:15.315
- Often when I meet people,

00:01:15.315 --> 00:01:19.435
the very first question I get is "Where are you from?"

00:01:19.435 --> 00:01:22.093
- It confuses people, because they usually associate

00:01:22.093 --> 00:01:24.247
being American with being white.

00:01:24.247 --> 00:01:26.893
They don't really know how to react,

00:01:26.893 --> 00:01:29.181
and it usually comes off as offensive.

00:01:29.181 --> 00:01:31.392
- They think that it'll give them some insight

00:01:31.392 --> 00:01:33.516
in to who I am as a person,

00:01:33.516 --> 00:01:36.014
my cultural identity is a part of me,

00:01:36.014 --> 00:01:39.752
but it doesn't affect who I am really as a person.

00:01:39.752 --> 00:01:42.585
- I was once on a date with a guy,

00:01:42.652 --> 00:01:46.152
and he asked the "What are you?" question.

00:01:46.891 --> 00:01:49.224
So I explained my ethnicity,

00:01:49.598 --> 00:01:52.740
and he was still kind of confused, and then,

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:55.973
mixing up the different types of Asian,

00:01:55.973 --> 00:01:58.279
and was like, "Oh, is your mom Chinese?"

00:01:58.279 --> 00:02:00.376
And I was like, I just said I was Japanese.

00:02:00.376 --> 00:02:03.028
- I was just like having lunch with one of my friends,

00:02:03.028 --> 00:02:06.608
and he introduced me to another friend of his,

00:02:06.608 --> 00:02:08.264
who also is from Thailand.

00:02:08.264 --> 00:02:11.755
He was like, "Oh yeah, this is my friend, Aaron. He's Thai."

00:02:11.755 --> 00:02:12.588
And

00:02:13.463 --> 00:02:15.046
She was like, "No."

00:02:15.784 --> 00:02:19.108
It was just annoying that that was the way that we met.

00:02:19.108 --> 00:02:20.806
- It not only makes me feel uncomfortable,

00:02:20.806 --> 00:02:23.720
but it makes me feel as if I'm sort of "other,"

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:26.787
and it just sort of just disconnects me,

00:02:26.787 --> 00:02:28.666
and feels like I'm taken out of the equation,

00:02:28.666 --> 00:02:30.513
and put in a specific box,

00:02:30.513 --> 00:02:32.763
and it feels really lonely.

00:02:34.404 --> 00:02:38.318
- There are times where it feels like the questions

00:02:38.318 --> 00:02:42.401
reflect their own inner stereotypes or prejudice.

00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:46.828
And there is the opportunity to help people through that,

00:02:46.828 --> 00:02:50.192
and help correct some of those misconceptions.

00:02:50.192 --> 00:02:52.624
- When I think about my grandmother,

00:02:52.624 --> 00:02:55.541
who survived and was able to endure

00:02:55.838 --> 00:02:58.266
so much when she was there, and then

00:02:58.266 --> 00:03:00.859
come to this country not speaking English,

00:03:00.859 --> 00:03:02.981
and be successful, and have a great life,

00:03:02.981 --> 00:03:04.914
and pass all of that on to me,

00:03:04.914 --> 00:03:06.269
I feel very very proud.

00:03:06.269 --> 00:03:08.031
- I'm proud to be multiracial,

00:03:08.031 --> 00:03:11.206
because I have two different cultures that I'm a part of.

00:03:11.206 --> 00:03:15.035
I'm no longer ashamed of not looking a certain way.

00:03:15.035 --> 00:03:18.363
^I feel like being multiracial is unique in its own sense.

00:03:18.363 --> 00:03:21.530
- More and more I'm seeing more people

00:03:22.392 --> 00:03:25.511
representing us out in the world, as far as

00:03:25.511 --> 00:03:28.261
actors or musicians or activists.

00:03:28.751 --> 00:03:30.697
To see other people who look like me,

00:03:30.697 --> 00:03:33.136
and have had the same experiences as me,

00:03:33.136 --> 00:03:36.449
making big changes out in the world is really inspiring.

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:39.445
- When my parents were young parents,

00:03:39.445 --> 00:03:42.952
it was still pretty rare to see mixed-race couples,

00:03:42.952 --> 00:03:45.822
people would ask my mom, "Oh, are you babysitting?"

00:03:45.822 --> 00:03:49.045
I'm proud of my parents for following their hearts

00:03:49.045 --> 00:03:52.545
and loving someone who there may have been

00:03:52.747 --> 00:03:55.806
social pressure to not love, and then also

00:03:55.806 --> 00:03:57.751
raising us with the understanding

00:03:57.751 --> 00:04:02.135
that love is not about a race, it's about who you love.

00:04:02.135 --> 00:04:05.322
- If I could give a message to someone just like me,

00:04:05.322 --> 00:04:08.991
I would tell them to not be ashamed of who they are,

00:04:08.991 --> 00:04:11.615
and to love all parts of themself,

00:04:11.615 --> 00:04:13.162
and where they come from.

00:04:13.162 --> 00:04:14.617
- You have to define for yourself

00:04:14.617 --> 00:04:17.200
what it means to be mixed race.

00:04:17.601 --> 00:04:20.736
Your individual experience of your own culture

00:04:20.736 --> 00:04:23.002
and your own family, your own history,

00:04:23.002 --> 00:04:27.815
and how all of that affects you today is totally up to you.

00:04:27.815 --> 00:04:32.057
- You are special and different but in a really awesome way,

00:04:32.057 --> 00:04:35.057
and if anyone tries to make you feel

00:04:35.090 --> 00:04:37.840
like that difference is not okay,

00:04:38.161 --> 00:04:39.578
or is other or is

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:41.780
bad in any way,

00:04:41.972 --> 00:04:43.892
you know just don't listen to them.

00:04:43.892 --> 00:04:45.309
- There would be periods in my life

00:04:45.309 --> 00:04:47.575
where I would try really hard

00:04:47.575 --> 00:04:50.075
to be just one part of myself.

00:04:50.666 --> 00:04:53.759
So there were phases where just I would try

00:04:53.759 --> 00:04:56.229
to just be very white, and then other times

00:04:56.229 --> 00:04:59.341
where I would try more to be like the Asian kids.

00:04:59.341 --> 00:05:01.911
And I think that's a part of finding your identity

00:05:01.911 --> 00:05:03.427
when you are mixed race.

00:05:03.427 --> 00:05:04.875
- You also need to find people,

00:05:04.875 --> 00:05:07.032
whether they're multiracial or not,

00:05:07.032 --> 00:05:09.965
who will celebrate you for who you are,

00:05:09.965 --> 00:05:12.648
and help you in your discovery of who you are,

00:05:12.648 --> 00:05:13.868
and who you want to be.

00:05:13.868 --> 00:05:17.735
- Sometimes when we talk about people who are multiracial,

00:05:17.735 --> 00:05:20.815
we talk about them as being part something,

00:05:20.815 --> 00:05:25.044
or being half something, and I know it's just words,

00:05:25.044 --> 00:05:29.984
but at the same time I feel like we should embrace the idea,

00:05:29.984 --> 00:05:32.999
that though your blood quantum may be

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:37.999
a certain amount of another group, it doesn't make you less.

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:39.940
You are a full Hawaiian.

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:41.204
You are a full Asian.

00:05:41.204 --> 00:05:43.204
You are a full European.

00:05:43.469 --> 00:05:46.134
You should be able to feel like a full member

00:05:46.134 --> 00:05:48.551
of all those different parts.

00:05:48.978 --> 00:05:51.895
(soft piano music)

